WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.200
-Set up a 20-meter perimeter.
-Roger that.

3
00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.440
Commander Berger. you know the procedure.

4
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.400
As of now. you're in custody.

5
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.640
Yeah.

6
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.880
ELITE FORCE

7
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.040
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I'm sure we'll resolve this quickly.

8
00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.680
I'd just like to clarify a few details.

9
00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.480
So. you left your phone
in the locker room?

10
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.240
Yes. I left my phone in the locker room.

11
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.000
It's unlike you to be unreachable.

12
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.760
It's also unlike me
to pay tribute to one of my partners.

13
00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.640
Maybe my mind was elsewhere.

14
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.800
On the anniversary
of your former partner's death.

15
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.320
you went to the site where he died.

16
00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.200
In the 15 years since his death.
have you ever made such a trip.

17
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.960
on that date. to that place?

18
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.640
No.

19
00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:03.880
Why this year?

20
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.760
Maybe because of Christophe's death.

21
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.800
-I felt the need to.
-The need to pay your respects?

22
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.680
Yes.

23
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.080
Armed with an AK-47 assault rifle
and a Kel-Tec shotgun.

24
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.400
I'm the cautious type.
Looks like I was right to be.

25
00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.000
I'm cautious too.

26
00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.640
But I don't bring a whole arsenal
to my father's grave.

27
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.200
Maybe the difference between us

28
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.040
lies in how dangerous our jobs are.

29
00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.920
Have you or your father ever been targeted

30
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.040
by a car bomb at work?

31
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.360
Have you and your father.
in the course of your work.

32
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.240
ever wondered
if you were going to make it home alive

33
00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.240
to kiss your family goodnight?

34
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.800
Maybe if your job
was a little more dangerous

35
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.680
than just handing out red cards
to people doing theirs…

36
00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.880
perhaps you'd see things differently.

37
00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.840
My father was a general
in the French Armed Forces.

38
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.840
But I understand what you're saying.

39
00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.680
What's strange is that
these weapons aren't registered anywhere.

40
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.960
No permits were ever issued.
They're ghost guns.

41
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.920
These weapons were seized
on a recent mission.

42
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.720
I followed protocol to register them.

43
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.120
I guess the paperwork got lost somewhere

44
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.440
in the maze of red tape.

45
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.880
Mea culpa.

46
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.440
Fine me.

47
00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.160
Please.

48
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.640
90 rounds of 7.62 mm ammo for the AK-47

49
00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.880
and 30 Brenneke rounds for the shotgun.

50
00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.680
I'm confused. Commander.

51
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.800
Is that standard ammunition
for these weapons?

52
00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.880
We choose ammunition
based on our missions.

53
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.040
You'd know that if you had
the slightest interest in our jobs.

54
00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.440
So. what kind of mission
requires Brenneke rounds?

55
00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.360
The kind requiring heavy firepower.

56
00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.000
So. armed with an assault rifle
and a shotgun.

57
00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.680
both unregistered
and therefore untraceable.

58
00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.160
with ammo chosen for maximum power.

59
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:19.280
you drove to the site
where your partner died.

60
00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.880
illegally entering a military facility.

61
00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.800
something you'd never done in 15 years.

62
00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:30.200
And then. by some tragic coincidence.
you ran into Mayard.

63
00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.840
the sole suspect in your boss' death.

64
00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.600
You arrested him.
and despite your expertise

65
00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.000
and your extensive experience
within the GIGN.

66
00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.360
he managed to grab a weapon
and you shot him. Is that correct?

67
00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.440
Minus the sarcasm. yes.

68
00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.360
I promised that if you crossed the line
one more time. I'd ensure it was the last.

69
00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.560
I will keep my promise.

70
00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.320
I can assure you.

71
00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:37.800
Yes.

72
00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.360
Mrs. Berger. come in.

73
00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:04.160
A police report. filed by
one of your daughter's classmates.

74
00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.560
regarding events that occurred
during a party at his home.

75
00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.800
He describes an altercation
between Manon Berger's father

76
00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.400
and several of his guests.

77
00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:17.360
If it were serious. the prosecutor
would've taken it up and filed charges.

78
00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.920
This is just a police report.

79
00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.200
Indeed. Pressured by his father.

80
00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.600
the young man withdrew his statement.
blaming it on the alcohol.

81
00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.480
The prosecutor was therefore
unable to take up the case.

82
00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:29.760
So? That doesn't explain why I'm here.

83
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.640
Your husband is trained in violence.

84
00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.480
He's an expert in every form of combat.
In short. he's a weapon.

85
00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.560
At 1:00 a.m.. your daughter
wasn't answering her phone.

86
00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.720
He panicked. When he found her…

87
00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.200
he tasered the guy.

88
00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.760
I have to wonder. Mrs. Berger.

89
00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.320
When his loved ones are involved.
just how far will your husband go?

90
00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.720
David's job is to protect.

91
00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.760
You. me. his daughter. everyone.

92
00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.400
His mission comes first. Always.

93
00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.160
It's called a work ethic.

94
00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:26.720
Does the premeditated killing of a suspect
fall under what you call a work ethic?

95
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.760
How long have you been working
with Commander Berger?

96
00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.880
Five years.

97
00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:35.960
A little longer.

98
00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.360
How would you describe his leadership?

99
00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:43.960
Exemplary.

100
00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:49.320
Would you say
you're close to Commander Berger?

101
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.800
You know. the GIGN is one big family.
We're all brothers in arms.

102
00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.840
There's no sound on this video.

103
00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:01.440
but do you remember what you said
to the Commander at that moment?

104
00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.320
Not really. no. The usual. I guess.

105
00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.560
Upcoming training. how our kids are doing.

106
00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.840
The bag looks particularly heavy.

107
00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.160
Do you have any idea what was in it?

108
00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.040
He left the armory with a bag.

109
00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.440
You know very well what's in it.
Why are you asking me?

110
00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:25.640
There was no target practice scheduled
and no operations that day.

111
00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:26.680
Why take weapons out?

112
00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.560
We're elite marksmen.
we take weapons in and out all the time.

113
00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.040
Nothing surprising there.

114
00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.920
Yet you look surprised in this footage.

115
00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.440
That's your interpretation.

116
00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:46.680
I think you knew the commander
wasn't going to training.

117
00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.280
I think you warned him.
You're an honest man.

118
00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.040
And because you're loyal.
you're keeping quiet today.

119
00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.440
But loyal to whom? That's the question
you need to ask yourself.

120
00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.800
To your men?

121
00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.000
Or to your friend?

122
00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.960
Do you think driving in the dead of night
to an abandoned military base.

123
00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.240
running into the suspect by chance.
heavily armed. then shooting him.

124
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.240
is the behavior
of a responsible GIGN leader?

125
00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.280
The commander made a choice.

126
00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:24.200
He chose personal revenge
at the expense of the entire GIGN.

127
00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.960
Not to mention the missing CL20 stock.

128
00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.800
We have no chance of ever finding it
now that the main suspect is dead.

129
00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.400
Now you. Major?

130
00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.000
What choice will you make?

131
00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.000
During the Kröller op.

132
00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:59.760
when we were attacked
by the sniper in the woods…

133
00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:05.080
I'm not sure what.

134
00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.160
But he brought something back.

135
00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.480
Where were you last night?

136
00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.080
I was at home. Alone. in my apartment.

137
00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:25.920
You weren't at home.

138
00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.200
You were there when he shot Mayard.

139
00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.640
You deliberately concealed your presence.

140
00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.640
You know what that means.

141
00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.160
Your career is over.

142
00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:28.760
Do you know what this is?

143
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.040
SEALED - DO NOT OPEN

144
00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.800
It looks like a cartridge case
used by the sniper

145
00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.280
who shot the arms dealer.

146
00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.880
Kröller.

147
00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.800
It was in your home.

148
00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.400
Can you explain why it was there?

149
00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.800
You know. long-range shooting
is one of my specialties.

150
00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.120
I've accumulated a lot of casings
over the years.

151
00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:02.480
Why do you think
we went as far as searching your home?

152
00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.240
Tenacity.

153
00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.360
Major Bonenfant. your colleague.
Your friend. even. Cédric.

154
00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:13.200
He told me about it.

155
00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.680
You are aware that removing evidence
from a crime scene

156
00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:18.680
is grounds for court-martial.

157
00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.520
Another coincidence?
Like the weapons you took from the armory.

158
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:27.760
Like being in the right place
at the right time to shoot the terrorist.

159
00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.800
I have another explanation.
As you might've guessed.

160
00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.720
On graduation night. Christophe.

161
00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:42.040
your superior. your mentor. the man
who taught you everything. is killed.

162
00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:44.880
Your world collapses.

163
00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.280
You start your own parallel investigation.

164
00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.880
You illegally interrogate a suspect
you just arrested.

165
00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:53.560
You take evidence from a crime scene.

166
00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:57.160
You track down Mayard.
but he slips away at the hospital.

167
00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:01.080
So. you go through
your Intel colleague's computer.

168
00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.960
You finally get a lead on the suspect.

169
00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.120
Your rogue investigation
becomes a revenge mission.

170
00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.000
Commander. may I speak with you?

171
00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.320
After every shot.
my men are detained. It's procedure.

172
00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.320
The police handle it.
I don't get involved.

173
00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.480
Now I find out that you. the IGGN.

174
00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:37.360
have been interrogating my men
since this morning?

175
00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.160
You even summoned David's wife?

176
00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:44.480
So I need to know
if you're just being overzealous

177
00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.000
or if I should be worried.

178
00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.000
Come with me.

179
00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:57.400
The SD card from your vehicle's dashcam

180
00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.960
has mysteriously disappeared.
Another coincidence.

181
00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:04.520
Luckily. the dashcams were just updated.
I triggered the recording remotely.

182
00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.600
The footage went straight to the server.

183
00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:07.880
Villiers?

184
00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:27.760
David.

185
00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:30.960
The question now is
whether you'll go to prison or not.

186
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.160
When did you decide to kill Mayard?

187
00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.640
What role did your mentee play
in your plans?

188
00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.120
Can I ask you to stop recording?

189
00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.840
And can Spielberg leave?

190
00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:05.640
I'll confess everything.
The murder. the premeditation. everything.

191
00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.600
But on two conditions.

192
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:12.080
First. Max stays out of this.

193
00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:14.720
He followed me. not knowing what I'd do.

194
00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.280
I forced him to stay quiet.
He's not involved.

195
00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:18.800
Second.

196
00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:22.920
let me go home tonight.

197
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.520
To see my family.

198
00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:27.120
And I'll confess tomorrow.

199
00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:31.240
Even when you've lost. you try to bend
the rules to your advantage.

200
00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.200
Why would I agree to that?

201
00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.760
Why wouldn't you agree to that?

202
00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:44.520
Right now. all you have is a lie
about Max's involvement in this.

203
00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:48.480
And a few minor offenses. Nothing much.

204
00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.920
It's enough to have you and Max
dismissed from the force.

205
00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.360
Yeah.

206
00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.240
But what would really make you happy?

207
00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.200
A mere dismissal?

208
00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.160
Or the chance to put me behind bars?

209
00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:19.280
-You good? Not too much adrenaline?
-We're all good.

210
00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.720
-Hey.
-How's it going?

211
00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.720
Hi.

212
00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:32.320
Here we go again. guys.

213
00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.080
Move out. let's go.

214
00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.880
Come on. bring it down! Keep going!

215
00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.640
Quick. let's go inside.

216
00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:44.560
Come on!

217
00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:46.760
It's in! Let's go!

218
00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:47.920
Police!

219
00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.320
Too slow. guys.

220
00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.480
Within ten seconds. they could be dead.

221
00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:55.680
Come on. let's go. Take a right.

222
00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:03.400
Go right!

223
00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:05.480
Move forward!

224
00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.360
Okay. stop.

225
00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.840
Guys. debrief in ten minutes.
Change and meet me at the command post.

226
00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.240
We're all behind you. okay?

227
00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:27.120
You okay. man?

228
00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:40.160
Hey. asshole.

229
00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.000
If you want to talk. I'm here. okay?

230
00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.920
I probably would've done the same.

231
00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.840
Where were you?

232
00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.800
I didn't come here to talk.

233
00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:25.200
Since when does the IGGN
interrogate wives?

234
00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:27.880
She's an overzealous commander.

235
00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.800
She thinks you executed the guy
who killed Christophe.

236
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.200
Custody is 24 hours.
Why did she let you out?

237
00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.800
Because I confessed.

238
00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:39.760
What?

239
00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:44.560
I made a deal with her.
I'll sign whatever she wants tomorrow.

240
00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:47.120
In return. she's letting me
spend the evening with you.

241
00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.040
The evening?

242
00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.200
What are you saying?
Did you kill him or not?

243
00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.120
I could have.

244
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.480
What the fuck are you doing?

245
00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.440
You'll end up in prison.

246
00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:05.680
Max is involved in this. isn't he?
You don't owe him anything.

247
00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:09.600
What about Manon?

248
00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.800
Do you think I'm happy about this?
Do you think it's easy for me?

249
00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:24.160
I have to do this.
For Max. I have to do this.

250
00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.760
It's pointless being here tonight
if you won't be tomorrow.

251
00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.400
Pointless.

252
00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:02.960
You're leaving?

253
00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:05.280
It was nice. I have to go.

254
00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:10.360
Wait. You can't just show up at my door
and not explain anything to me.

255
00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:14.000
I don't want to talk about it.

256
00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:15.840
It's about David. isn't it?

257
00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:18.640
Killing the terrorist.

258
00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.800
He emptied out his locker.

259
00:22:23.720 --> 00:22:24.880
I heard he got fired.

260
00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:30.640
David didn't shoot.

261
00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.600
I did.

262
00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:36.280
Wait. what?

263
00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:41.640
What are you talking about?

264
00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:44.960
I was with David. I followed him.

265
00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:49.240
We arrested the terrorist together.
It went wrong.

266
00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:52.080
I screwed up.

267
00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:02.240
So why is David being fired
if you're the one who shot the gun?

268
00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:05.120
He told the IGGN that he was alone.

269
00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:06.600
That I wasn't there.

270
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.480
He's taking the fall for me.

271
00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:12.320
You're letting him?

272
00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:13.920
He's lied to me from the start.

273
00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:18.120
Before Mayard died. he said
David was to blame for my dad's death.

274
00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:21.280
Does that justify him taking the fall?

275
00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:23.280
He deserves to be punished.

276
00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.520
Yeah. he does.

277
00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:28.560
But not like this.

278
00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.760
-I'm going to tell her the truth.
-Don't. Look at me.

279
00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:17.360
If you do. your career is over.

280
00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:20.000
My career is behind me.

281
00:24:20.080 --> 00:24:21.480
It's…

282
00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:29.360
About my dad. Mayard says it's your fault.
You say it's not.

283
00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:31.920
You're ready to ruin your life for me.

284
00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.120
A month ago. you forgot I even existed.

285
00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:36.200
Max…

286
00:24:36.280 --> 00:24:38.040
It must be because you feel guilty.

287
00:24:38.760 --> 00:24:40.600
Explain why you're risking it all.

288
00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:43.080
or I'll walk in there
and tell them the truth.

289
00:24:59.880 --> 00:25:03.320
Lone terrorist.
Former lab staff. idealistic type.

290
00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:06.440
He wants all of France to see
the weapons they're designing here.

291
00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:08.440
All I know is that it's explosives.

292
00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:10.200
Same partners as usual.

293
00:25:10.280 --> 00:25:11.680
Usual rules of engagement.

294
00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:15.840
Self-defense. hostage in danger.
or a direct order.

295
00:25:15.920 --> 00:25:18.160
Okay. everyone? Let's go.

296
00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:19.680
All right. let's go. guys.

297
00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:32.320
Christophe. I want to change partners.

298
00:25:33.600 --> 00:25:34.440
On what grounds?

299
00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:36.840
It's for the best.

300
00:25:39.200 --> 00:25:42.160
You two. I don't know what the issue is.
but I'll be brief.

301
00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:45.160
There's a terrorist
and 21 hostages who need us.

302
00:25:45.240 --> 00:25:49.120
Don't make me regret
having you in this section. Do your job.

303
00:25:51.120 --> 00:25:51.960
Okay.

304
00:26:01.480 --> 00:26:02.320
My daughter.

305
00:26:02.400 --> 00:26:03.680
Evacuate!

306
00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:05.480
Doc! Over here!

307
00:26:05.560 --> 00:26:08.920
I'm a dad too. ma'am. I'm a dad too.
I'll go get your daughter.

308
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:10.400
My daughter is in the lab!

309
00:26:10.480 --> 00:26:12.520
-Everybody. we're evacuating!
-No. wait!

310
00:26:16.160 --> 00:26:17.680
This way!

311
00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:25.800
We need to be out of here in 50 seconds.

312
00:26:25.880 --> 00:26:29.040
Lina!

313
00:26:29.120 --> 00:26:30.680
Everyone. evacuate!

314
00:26:30.760 --> 00:26:34.520
-Lina. we're with your parents!
-David. Laurent! Get out of there.

315
00:26:35.200 --> 00:26:37.240
-Lina!
-Initiating emergency procedure.

316
00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:39.880
-Lina!
-Do you copy? Get out of there now!

317
00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:42.200
Lina. if you're hiding.
you need to come out!

318
00:26:43.200 --> 00:26:44.360
-David.
-Lina!

319
00:26:44.440 --> 00:26:46.080
-I can't wait any longer.
-Lina!

320
00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:52.040
Laurent. we need to leave. damn it.
We need to get out of here!

321
00:26:52.120 --> 00:26:53.360
It's an order! Out!

322
00:26:53.440 --> 00:26:56.160
-We have to go.
-We won't leave until we find her. Lina!

323
00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:58.000
-We need to fucking leave!
-Lina!

324
00:26:58.080 --> 00:27:01.200
-Come on.
-Let go of me. damn it!

325
00:27:02.560 --> 00:27:05.120
Get your hands off me!

326
00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:07.600
She's not here. It's about to blow up.
We need to go.

327
00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:09.880
Get out of here then!

328
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:27.040
Fuck!

329
00:27:35.080 --> 00:27:37.520
David. Look at me.

330
00:27:39.560 --> 00:27:40.560
Get out. David.

331
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:43.640
-There has to be another way out.
-It's over.

332
00:27:44.320 --> 00:27:46.800
We both know it. Get out of here. please.

333
00:27:48.360 --> 00:27:49.400
Please.

334
00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:57.360
I'm sorry. Laurent.

335
00:27:58.360 --> 00:27:59.600
I'm sorry.

336
00:28:05.320 --> 00:28:06.440
Take care of Max for me.

337
00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:10.760
Go on. get out.

338
00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:14.280
Get out of here!

339
00:28:41.400 --> 00:28:43.320
I knew you were still here.

340
00:28:46.960 --> 00:28:48.120
My name is Laurent.

341
00:28:49.360 --> 00:28:50.480
Will you come with me?

342
00:29:01.160 --> 00:29:02.480
It's going to be okay.

343
00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:06.000
Is Mommy coming to get me?

344
00:29:06.080 --> 00:29:06.960
Yes. she is.

345
00:29:25.680 --> 00:29:27.360
There's one thing I don't get.

346
00:29:29.280 --> 00:29:32.720
If you're not to blame for his death.
why do all this for me?

347
00:29:36.480 --> 00:29:38.520
Because it's still kind of my fault.

348
00:29:40.040 --> 00:29:43.400
I mean. the fact that
Laurent was so angry that day

349
00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:45.520
was partly my fault.

350
00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:50.680
He'd just received some test results.

351
00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:56.640
He found out he couldn't have children.

352
00:29:58.680 --> 00:30:00.000
That he never could.

353
00:30:03.800 --> 00:30:07.560
I kept it secret all these years
at your mother's request. but…

354
00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:11.160
I couldn't do it anymore.

355
00:30:13.560 --> 00:30:14.760
I am your father.

356
00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:24.760
Listen.

357
00:30:24.840 --> 00:30:28.360
I know I haven't been there for you
since Laurent died. I…

358
00:30:28.880 --> 00:30:31.360
Your mother wanted me to stay away.
and I get that.

359
00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:34.200
Maybe I was an idiot for listening to her.
I don't know.

360
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:40.040
I can't go back in time.
I can't change the past.

361
00:30:41.760 --> 00:30:43.880
But there is something I can do now.

362
00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:46.240
For you.

363
00:30:50.800 --> 00:30:52.240
I can protect you now.

364
00:30:56.280 --> 00:30:57.640
Major Villiers?

365
00:30:59.440 --> 00:31:01.040
We weren't expecting you.

366
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.000
I need to talk to you.

367
00:31:10.840 --> 00:31:11.760
Come in.

368
00:31:38.800 --> 00:31:40.560
I'll tell you what really happened.

369
00:31:54.720 --> 00:31:56.160
Give me five minutes.

370
00:32:23.160 --> 00:32:24.880
Hi. sweetheart. How are you?

371
00:32:24.960 --> 00:32:26.440
You lied to me.

372
00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:28.280
What do you mean?

373
00:32:30.400 --> 00:32:31.680
About Dad. About David.

374
00:32:32.600 --> 00:32:34.000
How could you do that?

375
00:32:35.040 --> 00:32:39.160
Wait. Where are you?
Let's talk about it. okay?

376
00:32:39.240 --> 00:32:40.120
No.

377
00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:42.280
Tell me where you are.

378
00:32:43.040 --> 00:32:43.960
Max.

379
00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:47.880
Max. please. tell me where you are.

380
00:32:49.200 --> 00:32:50.120
Max?

381
00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:52.640
Gentlemen. ready to come back in?

382
00:32:59.760 --> 00:33:00.680
Shit.

383
00:33:03.080 --> 00:33:07.080
I have rarely seen so many breaches
of procedure. GIGN ethics. and the law.

384
00:33:07.160 --> 00:33:10.680
You played vigilante.
tried to arrest him. and he died.

385
00:33:10.760 --> 00:33:13.360
Granted. it was self-defense. but he died.

386
00:33:13.440 --> 00:33:17.080
If I had my way. you'd be convicted.
A suspended sentence at the very least.

387
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:19.600
And probably prison time.

388
00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:22.720
But it seems
it would serve no one's interests.

389
00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:25.240
neither the GIGN's. nor the gendarmerie's.

390
00:33:25.320 --> 00:33:26.720
for the two heroic officers

391
00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:30.760
who stopped a bomber's deadly rampage
to be publicly sanctioned.

392
00:33:31.920 --> 00:33:34.200
-Isn't that right. General?
-Yes.

393
00:33:34.280 --> 00:33:38.360
That said. your actions have no place
in the gendarmerie. let alone the GIGN.

394
00:33:38.440 --> 00:33:41.240
Commander. I expected better from you.

395
00:33:41.320 --> 00:33:44.440
You dragged a young recruit
into a clandestine operation.

396
00:33:44.520 --> 00:33:46.840
You're suspended pending early retirement.

397
00:33:46.920 --> 00:33:49.000
You won't set foot in the barracks again.

398
00:33:49.080 --> 00:33:52.960
Major Villiers. your inexperience
does not excuse your poor judgment.

399
00:33:53.040 --> 00:33:55.320
The board will decide your fate
within two weeks.

400
00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:57.920
Until then.
you may not participate in operations

401
00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:00.400
or in training
without your section leader's approval.

402
00:34:01.000 --> 00:34:03.720
The 500 kilos of explosives
are still out there.

403
00:34:04.360 --> 00:34:07.320
I don't know what outcome will be.
but I'll be blunt.

404
00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:10.080
You do not belong at the GIGN.

405
00:34:11.120 --> 00:34:12.200
You're dismissed.

406
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:26.640
Max!

407
00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:32.800
What else do you want to say?

408
00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:36.680
I gave everything to be part of the GIGN.

409
00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:40.520
All I wanted was to be like you and Dad!

410
00:34:41.560 --> 00:34:45.080
But all that is bullshit!
You're not heroes! It's bullshit!

411
00:35:55.720 --> 00:35:58.360
My love. do you know
where Daddy's office is?

412
00:36:00.040 --> 00:36:03.480
Go there. hide. and don't make a sound.

413
00:36:03.560 --> 00:36:06.120
Don't come out until you hear my voice.

414
00:36:06.840 --> 00:36:09.960
Do you understand?
I'll come get you. I promise.

415
00:36:10.560 --> 00:36:11.680
What about you?

416
00:36:13.200 --> 00:36:15.040
Don't worry. you know us.

417
00:36:15.120 --> 00:36:18.040
We're strong. We'll fight. We'll win.

418
00:36:18.120 --> 00:36:21.760
When I say "run." you go.
Do you understand? I'll come get you.

419
00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:32.680
Alright. go. sweetie.

420
00:36:33.280 --> 00:36:34.160
Run.

421
00:36:35.640 --> 00:36:37.720
-Go on.
-Go. Run!

422
00:36:53.360 --> 00:36:54.560
Keep calm.

423
00:37:05.160 --> 00:37:08.360
You! Get up! Now!

424
00:37:08.440 --> 00:37:10.040
Goddammit!

425
00:37:12.200 --> 00:37:13.320
Fuck!

426
00:37:19.400 --> 00:37:20.560
Police!

427
00:37:20.640 --> 00:37:22.440
Stay with me.

428
00:37:31.120 --> 00:37:34.040
I'm a dad too. ma'am.
I'll go get your daughter.

429
00:37:34.120 --> 00:37:35.240
Everyone. evacuate!

430
00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:37.920
I'll come get you. I promise.

431
00:38:09.160 --> 00:38:12.560
DANGER EXPLOSIVES
CL20

432
00:38:29.560 --> 00:38:31.640
A HUMAN TRAGEDY AMID STATE SECRETS

433
00:38:31.720 --> 00:38:33.640
NINE-YEAR-OLD LINA MAYARD
A LIFE CUT SHORT

434
00:39:15.960 --> 00:39:19.800
Okay. You can sleep over at Nina's
on one condition. Practice your pieces.

435
00:39:19.880 --> 00:39:20.880
And don't go out.

436
00:39:20.960 --> 00:39:24.680
We're going to the conservatory.
then we'll go straight to Nina's.

437
00:39:24.760 --> 00:39:26.680
-Bye. Mom. I love you.
-I love you too.

438
00:39:41.840 --> 00:39:42.920
I've been suspended.

439
00:39:43.440 --> 00:39:44.360
What?

440
00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:47.400
I told Max everything.

441
00:39:49.080 --> 00:39:50.800
I told him I was his father.

442
00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:57.800
The idiot still decided to talk
to the inspector.

443
00:39:57.880 --> 00:40:00.280
even though everything
was going to be just fine.

444
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:05.520
Going to prison to protect him
would've been just fine?

445
00:40:05.600 --> 00:40:07.200
What would've been fine about that?

446
00:40:08.840 --> 00:40:11.320
Jess. you know
I made a promise to Laurent.

447
00:40:11.400 --> 00:40:13.880
Before he died.
I promised I'd take care of Max.

448
00:40:13.960 --> 00:40:16.680
I promised him that I'd take care of Max.

449
00:40:16.760 --> 00:40:18.160
I promised him.

450
00:40:18.240 --> 00:40:23.120
COMMIT FOR LIFE

451
00:40:31.960 --> 00:40:34.360
You really think
that's why you're doing all this?

452
00:40:35.840 --> 00:40:37.120
That's bullshit.

453
00:40:37.200 --> 00:40:40.120
Even if you hadn't promised.
you'd be doing the same thing.

454
00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:43.880
Because the truth is. you feel so guilty.

455
00:40:43.960 --> 00:40:46.840
You don't know what else to do
to stop blaming yourself.

456
00:40:48.960 --> 00:40:51.600
When are you going to let yourself live?

457
00:40:51.680 --> 00:40:54.280
When are you going to make time for us?

458
00:40:54.840 --> 00:40:56.440
You're not guilty of anything.

459
00:40:56.520 --> 00:40:57.960
I am guilty.

460
00:41:00.200 --> 00:41:02.560
I'm guilty of betraying Laurent.

461
00:41:04.560 --> 00:41:08.160
I'm guilty of putting him in that state
just before the op. I am.

462
00:41:09.720 --> 00:41:12.240
I'm guilty of not being there for Max.

463
00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:21.440
I wasn't there for him. for fuck's sake.
He's my son. I wasn't there for him.

464
00:41:28.200 --> 00:41:31.760
And the truth is.
I'm not fucking there for you guys either.

465
00:41:33.480 --> 00:41:36.800
I'm there for everyone else.
but my family always comes last.

466
00:42:04.800 --> 00:42:06.040
I'm sorry.

467
00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:09.440
I'm sorry.

468
00:43:19.200 --> 00:43:20.400
I'm sorry.

469
00:48:41.240 --> 00:48:46.240
Subtitle translation by: Alison Simpson

469
00:48:47.305 --> 00:49:47.271
